{
  "_doc": "The fish of the world's waters (user 2026-09-27: 'add a fish powerlevel with different types of fish', 'we should have actual fish in the ponds and rivers with there own intelligence we mimic and try to catch'). `waters`: the most of each species a square's water holds (its type's `water` in squares.json: river, brook, spring, lake, marsh), fish as the player could see and catch them across the square (FishStock keeps the numbers; FishLife puts the ones near the player in the water, each with its own mind). `species`: how each lives (habitat, time of day, wariness, food, runs) and looks (FishMesh; tools/wildlife/fish_bake.gd bakes the meshes and skins). Species and seasons are the northeastern woodlands' of the 1760s (Lake Ontario's and the Ohio's waters); [H] marks what wants checking against a source.",
  "_habitat": "Where in the water a fish keeps its lie: seam (the slack water beside and behind a boulder or at a rapid's edge, where the current brings food), head (the head of a pool, just below a rapid), riffle (the fast shallow water of a rapid itself), pool (the slow deep middle), bank (slow water along the edges, under the banks). Layer: where in the water it swims (bottom, low, mid).",
  "_activity": "How active (feeding, moving, taking bait) it is by the time of day: dawn (05-08), day, dusk (18-21), night; x the month's (winter slow).",
  "_runs": "A run: in `months` (1-12) the square's water holds `in` of its most, out of them `out` (salmon up the rivers from the lake in the fall, suckers in the spring, sturgeon to the rapids in May and June). Between, the numbers drift toward it (FishStock).",
  "_barbels": "Barbels: [along the body, to the side, up] from the snout, fractions of its length, mirrored to both sides.",
  "_wary": "wary_m: how near a person standing on the bank at the water's edge a fish lets come before it bolts (crouched, still, farther off: nearer); fish fished hard grow warier (FishStock.wary).",
  "_bait": "Bait: picky (how much a dragged, unnatural drift puts it off: the power of `natural`), hold_s (how long it keeps a bait in its mouth before spitting it: the angler's time to set the hook), fight_s (how long it fights on the line before it tires, held lightly).",
